</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the output of <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is the output of the reduce predecessor of <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (which is <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>),
and <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant input (such as program input).
<math id="S4.SS1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{j}</annotation></semantics></math> does not index <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the reduce loops for both <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Eq. <a href="#S4.E2" title="In 4.1. Rolling Update ‣ 4. Template-Guided Optimizer ‣ Neptune: Advanced ML Operator Fusion for Locality and Parallelism on GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> assumes one reduce predecessor <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and one constant input <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>
for simplicity.
If there are multiple reduce predecessors and constant inputs,
they are added to the arguments of <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> without affecting the structure of the pattern.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Finding the Repair Function.</span>
Rolling update now solves for a <span id="S4.SS1.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">repair function</span>
that it will use to repair <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and produce a correct program.
A correct program is one where the fused <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> produces the same result as in the original program.
The intuition of how the repair function works comes from Eq. <a href="#S2.Ex7" title="In 2. Motivation ‣ Neptune: Advanced ML Operator Fusion for Locality and Parallelism on GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>
in the motivating example,
where we have demonstrated the <span id="S4.SS1.p8.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">tag-updating</span> behavior of the repair term.
We now generalize from the example and formalize this behavior.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">In Eq. <a href="#S2.Ex7" title="In 2. Motivation ‣ Neptune: Advanced ML Operator Fusion for Locality and Parallelism on GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the repair term is computed from
<math id="S4.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of the previous and current iterations,
and multiplies with <math id="S4.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{\langle j-1\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{\langle j-1\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math> to tag-update it.
Generalizing from the example, we see a repair function <math id="S4.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(t,r,r^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(t,r,r^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>
that accepts three arguments:
the value of <math id="S4.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}[\phi_{t}(\boldsymbol{i})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}[\phi_{t}(\boldsymbol{i})]</annotation></semantics></math> to be tag-updated,
and the value of <math id="S4.SS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]</annotation></semantics></math> in the previous (as <math id="S4.SS1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>) and current (as <math id="S4.SS1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>) iterations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Since tag-update involves modifying the tags on <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> inside the expression of <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,
it helps to have the explicit expression of <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> before we formally describe tag-updating.
In Eq. <a href="#S2.Ex7" title="In 2. Motivation ‣ Neptune: Advanced ML Operator Fusion for Locality and Parallelism on GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, every <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{\langle j\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{\langle j\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math> is an expression <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}^{\langle j\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}^{\langle j\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math>
with the same tag <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>.
Taking that to our general notation, we get the explicit form of <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.1523,0.5078,0.0898}X_{t}[\phi_{t}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\boldsymbol{j}\rangle}}=\mathcal{R}\left(f,0\preceq\boldsymbol{j}^{\prime}\preceq\boldsymbol{j},g(X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\boldsymbol{j}\rangle},C[\phi_{c}(\boldsymbol{i},\boldsymbol{j})])\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117">X</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117">t</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117" stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117">ϕ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117">t</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117">𝒊</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117">𝒋</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><msup><mi>𝒋</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⪯</mo><mi>𝒋</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝒋</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒋</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.1523,0.5078,0.0898}X_{t}[\phi_{t}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\boldsymbol{j}\rangle}}=\mathcal{R}\left(f,0\preceq\boldsymbol{j}^{\prime}\preceq\boldsymbol{j},g(X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\boldsymbol{j}\rangle},C[\phi_{c}(\boldsymbol{i},\boldsymbol{j})])\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p10.2" class="ltx_p">This expression (with <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0.1523,0.5078,0.0898}X_{t}[\phi_{t}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\boldsymbol{j}\rangle}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117">X</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117">ϕ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117">𝒊</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#278117;" mathcolor="#278117">𝒋</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0.1523,0.5078,0.0898}X_{t}[\phi_{t}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\boldsymbol{j}\rangle}}</annotation></semantics></math> in color)
generalizes Eq. <a href="#S2.Ex7" title="In 2. Motivation ‣ Neptune: Advanced ML Operator Fusion for Locality and Parallelism on GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
It is the result we <span id="S4.SS1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">want</span> to compute, not what the current program computes. It leads us to the definition of tag-updating:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_theorem">Definition 4.1.</h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A function <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">tag-updating</span> if it satisfies</p>
<table id="S4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall\boldsymbol{j}\in\mathcal{D}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝒋</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall\boldsymbol{j}\in\mathcal{D}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\ .\ h\left(\mathcal{R}(f,0\preceq\boldsymbol{j}^{\prime}\preceq\boldsymbol{j},g(X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\boldsymbol{j}\rangle},C[\phi_{c}(\boldsymbol{i},\boldsymbol{j})])),\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">.</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><msup><mi>𝒋</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⪯</mo><mi>𝒋</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝒋</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒋</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ .\ h\left(\mathcal{R}(f,0\preceq\boldsymbol{j}^{\prime}\preceq\boldsymbol{j},g(X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\boldsymbol{j}\rangle},C[\phi_{c}(\boldsymbol{i},\boldsymbol{j})])),\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\left.X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\boldsymbol{j}\rangle},X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\operatorname{next}(\boldsymbol{j})\rangle}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="2.000em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝒋</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>next</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒋</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\left.X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\boldsymbol{j}\rangle},X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\operatorname{next}(\boldsymbol{j})\rangle}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{R}\left(f,0\preceq\boldsymbol{j}^{\prime}\preceq\boldsymbol{j},g(X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\operatorname{next}(\boldsymbol{j})\rangle},C[\phi_{c}(\boldsymbol{i},\boldsymbol{j})])\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><msup><mi>𝒋</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⪯</mo><mi>𝒋</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>next</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒋</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒋</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{R}\left(f,0\preceq\boldsymbol{j}^{\prime}\preceq\boldsymbol{j},g(X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\operatorname{next}(\boldsymbol{j})\rangle},C[\phi_{c}(\boldsymbol{i},\boldsymbol{j})])\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">This definition shows that <math id="S4.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> tag-updates through a reduce expression that has repeated uses of <math id="S4.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.
We propose the following sufficient conditions that are simpler:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Theorem 4.2.</h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If a function <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the following two conditions, then it is tag-updating:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h\left(g(r,c),r,r^{\prime}\right)=g(r^{\prime},c)\hskip 9.24994pt\forall r,r^{\prime},c\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="1.097em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒳</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h\left(g(r,c),r,r^{\prime}\right)=g(r^{\prime},c)\hskip 9.24994pt\forall r,r^{\prime},c\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h\left(x\ \hbox to10.43pt{\vbox to10.43pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 5.21538pt\lower-5.21538pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke=#000000} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#000000} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width=0.4pt} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {{{}}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\hbox{\hbox{{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {{}{{{}}}{{}}{}{}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{}{}{}{}{}{{}\lxSVG@stroke\lxSVG@drawpath@unclipped{M 6.94 0 C 6.94 3.83 3.83 6.94 0 6.94 C -3.83 6.94 -6.94 3.83 -6.94 0 C -6.94 -3.83 -3.83 -6.94 0 -6.94 C 3.83 -6.94 6.94 -3.83 6.94 0 Z M 0 0}{fill:none} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces
}{{{{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}}\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@transformcm{1.0}{0.0}{0.0}{1.0}{-2.48265pt}{-2.0pt}\lxSVG@begingroup@{transform=matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.44 -2.77)} \pgfsys@hbox{58}\lxSVG@closescope }}}
\lxSVG@closescope }}}
}
\lxSVG@closescope {{{}}}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\hss}\lxSVG@discardpath\lxSVG@closescope \hss}}\lxSVG@closescope\endpgfpicture}}\ y,r,r^{\prime}\right)=h(x,r,r^{\prime})\ \hbox to10.43pt{\vbox to10.43pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 5.21538pt\lower-5.21538pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke=#000000} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#000000} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width=0.4pt} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {{{}}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\hbox{\hbox{{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {{}{{{}}}{{}}{}{}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{}{}{}{}{}{{}\lxSVG@stroke\lxSVG@drawpath@unclipped{M 6.94 0 C 6.94 3.83 3.83 6.94 0 6.94 C -3.83 6.94 -6.94 3.83 -6.94 0 C -6.94 -3.83 -3.83 -6.94 0 -6.94 C 3.83 -6.94 6.94 -3.83 6.94 0 Z M 0 0}{fill:none} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces
}{{{{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}}\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@transformcm{1.0}{0.0}{0.0}{1.0}{-2.48265pt}{-2.0pt}\lxSVG@begingroup@{transform=matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.44 -2.77)} \pgfsys@hbox{58}\lxSVG@closescope }}}
\lxSVG@closescope }}}
}
\lxSVG@closescope {{{}}}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\hss}\lxSVG@discardpath\lxSVG@closescope \hss}}\lxSVG@closescope\endpgfpicture}}\ h(y,r,r^{\prime})\hskip 9.24994pt\forall x,y,r,r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mo lspace="0.460em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-4.45px" height="14.43" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 14.43 14.43" width="14.43"> <g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,14.43) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(7.22,0) translate(0,7.22)"> <path style="fill:none" d="M 6.94 0 C 6.94 3.83 3.83 6.94 0 6.94 C -3.83 6.94 -6.94 3.83 -6.94 0 C -6.94 -3.83 -3.83 -6.94 0 -6.94 C 3.83 -6.94 6.94 -3.83 6.94 0 Z M 0 0"></path> <g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.44 -2.77)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.58em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="6.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mi mathsize="0.800em">f</mi></span></span></foreignObject> </g> </g> </svg> </mtext><mo lspace="0.460em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.460em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-4.45px" height="14.43" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 14.43 14.43" width="14.43"> <g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,14.43) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(7.22,0) translate(0,7.22)"> <path style="fill:none" d="M 6.94 0 C 6.94 3.83 3.83 6.94 0 6.94 C -3.83 6.94 -6.94 3.83 -6.94 0 C -6.94 -3.83 -3.83 -6.94 0 -6.94 C 3.83 -6.94 6.94 -3.83 6.94 0 Z M 0 0"></path> <g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.44 -2.77)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.58em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="6.87"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mi mathsize="0.800em">f</mi></span></span></foreignObject> </g> </g> </svg> </mtext><mo lspace="0.460em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="1.097em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒳</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h\left(x\ \hbox to10.43pt{\vbox to10.43pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 5.21538pt\lower-5.21538pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke=#000000} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#000000} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width=0.4pt} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {{{}}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\hbox{\hbox{{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {{}{{{}}}{{}}{}{}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{}{}{}{}{}{{}\lxSVG@stroke\lxSVG@drawpath@unclipped{M 6.94 0 C 6.94 3.83 3.83 6.94 0 6.94 C -3.83 6.94 -6.94 3.83 -6.94 0 C -6.94 -3.83 -3.83 -6.94 0 -6.94 C 3.83 -6.94 6.94 -3.83 6.94 0 Z M 0 0}{fill:none} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces
}{{{{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}}\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@transformcm{1.0}{0.0}{0.0}{1.0}{-2.48265pt}{-2.0pt}\lxSVG@begingroup@{transform=matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.44 -2.77)} \pgfsys@hbox{58}\lxSVG@closescope }}}
\lxSVG@closescope }}}
}
\lxSVG@closescope {{{}}}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\hss}\lxSVG@discardpath\lxSVG@closescope \hss}}\lxSVG@closescope\endpgfpicture}}\ y,r,r^{\prime}\right)=h(x,r,r^{\prime})\ \hbox to10.43pt{\vbox to10.43pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 5.21538pt\lower-5.21538pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke=#000000} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#000000} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width=0.4pt} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {{{}}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\hbox{\hbox{{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {{}{{{}}}{{}}{}{}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{}{}{}{}{}{{}\lxSVG@stroke\lxSVG@drawpath@unclipped{M 6.94 0 C 6.94 3.83 3.83 6.94 0 6.94 C -3.83 6.94 -6.94 3.83 -6.94 0 C -6.94 -3.83 -3.83 -6.94 0 -6.94 C 3.83 -6.94 6.94 -3.83 6.94 0 Z M 0 0}{fill:none} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces
}{{{{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}}\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@transformcm{1.0}{0.0}{0.0}{1.0}{-2.48265pt}{-2.0pt}\lxSVG@begingroup@{transform=matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.44 -2.77)} \pgfsys@hbox{58}\lxSVG@closescope }}}
\lxSVG@closescope }}}
}
\lxSVG@closescope {{{}}}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\hss}\lxSVG@discardpath\lxSVG@closescope \hss}}\lxSVG@closescope\endpgfpicture}}\ h(y,r,r^{\prime})\hskip 9.24994pt\forall x,y,r,r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
