</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Namely, <math id="S4.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> replaces the <math id="S4.SS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> argument of <math id="S4.SS1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> commutes with the reducer <math id="S4.SS1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>.
On algorithm line <a href="#algorithm1" title="In 4.1. Rolling Update ‣ 4. Template-Guided Optimizer ‣ Neptune: Advanced ML Operator Fusion for Locality and Parallelism on GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, rolling update solves Eq. <a href="#S4.E4" title="In Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.1. Rolling Update ‣ 4. Template-Guided Optimizer ‣ Neptune: Advanced ML Operator Fusion for Locality and Parallelism on GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> to find <math id="S4.SS1.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>,
and then proves Eq. <a href="#S4.E5" title="In Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.1. Rolling Update ‣ 4. Template-Guided Optimizer ‣ Neptune: Advanced ML Operator Fusion for Locality and Parallelism on GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> for this <math id="S4.SS1.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> on line <a href="#algorithm1" title="In 4.1. Rolling Update ‣ 4. Template-Guided Optimizer ‣ Neptune: Advanced ML Operator Fusion for Locality and Parallelism on GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
We further have the following result on how to solve Eq. <a href="#S4.E4" title="In Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.1. Rolling Update ‣ 4. Template-Guided Optimizer ‣ Neptune: Advanced ML Operator Fusion for Locality and Parallelism on GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Theorem 4.3.</h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=g(x,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=g(x,c)</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible in the second argument <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> to yield <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=g_{c}^{-1}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=g_{c}^{-1}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>,
then Eq. <a href="#S4.E4" title="In Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.1. Rolling Update ‣ 4. Template-Guided Optimizer ‣ Neptune: Advanced ML Operator Fusion for Locality and Parallelism on GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> has a solution:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(t,r,r^{\prime})=g(r^{\prime},g_{c}^{-1}(r,t))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(t,r,r^{\prime})=g(r^{\prime},g_{c}^{-1}(r,t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3. ‣ 4.1. Rolling Update ‣ 4. Template-Guided Optimizer ‣ Neptune: Advanced ML Operator Fusion for Locality and Parallelism on GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> allows us to find <math id="S4.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> explicitly
using symbolic solvers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>)</cite>.
An intuitive explanation of Eq. <a href="#S4.E6" title="In Theorem 4.3. ‣ 4.1. Rolling Update ‣ 4. Template-Guided Optimizer ‣ Neptune: Advanced ML Operator Fusion for Locality and Parallelism on GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> is that
the <math id="S4.SS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{c}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{c}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> term recovers the constant input read from the <math id="S4.SS1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> array,
before we apply <math id="S4.SS1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> with the updated <math id="S4.SS1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to get the new <math id="S4.SS1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> output.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Applying the Repair Function.</span>
Since we have found an <math id="S4.SS1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> that tag-updates <math id="S4.SS1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we apply it to the <math id="S4.SS1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> of the previous iteration,
i.e., we rewrite Eq. <a href="#S4.E2" title="In 4.1. Rolling Update ‣ 4. Template-Guided Optimizer ‣ Neptune: Advanced ML Operator Fusion for Locality and Parallelism on GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> into</p>
<table id="S4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{t}[\phi_{t}(\boldsymbol{i})]=\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{t}[\phi_{t}(\boldsymbol{i})]=\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h\left(X_{t}[\phi_{t}(\boldsymbol{i})],X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\operatorname{prev}(\boldsymbol{j})\rangle},X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\boldsymbol{j}\rangle}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>prev</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒋</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝒋</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h\left(X_{t}[\phi_{t}(\boldsymbol{i})],X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\operatorname{prev}(\boldsymbol{j})\rangle},X_{r}[\phi_{r}(\boldsymbol{i})]^{\langle\boldsymbol{j}\rangle}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \hbox to10.43pt{\vbox to10.43pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 5.21538pt\lower-5.21538pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke=#000000} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#000000} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width=0.4pt} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {{{}}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\hbox{\hbox{{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {{}{{{}}}{{}}{}{}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{}{}{}{}{}{{}\lxSVG@stroke\lxSVG@drawpath@unclipped{M 6.94 0 C 6.94 3.83 3.83 6.94 0 6.94 C -3.83 6.94 -6.94 3.83 -6.94 0 C -6.94 -3.83 -3.83 -6.94 0 -6.94 C 3.83 -6.94 6.94 -3.83 6.94 0 Z M 0 0}{fill:none} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces
