\lxSVG@closescope {{{}}}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\hss}\lxSVG@discardpath\lxSVG@closescope \hss}}\lxSVG@closescope\endpgfpicture}}\ h\left(X_{t,l}[\phi_{t,l}(\boldsymbol{i})],X_{r,l}[\phi_{r,l}(\boldsymbol{i})],X_{r,g}[\phi_{r,g}(\boldsymbol{i})]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">The first line is the body of the global nest <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}^{\text{global}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>global</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}^{\text{global}}</annotation></semantics></math> before the rewrite,
and the second line is after the rewrite.
<math id="S4.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t,g}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t,l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t,l}</annotation></semantics></math> are the output tensors of <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}^{\text{global}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>global</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}^{\text{global}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}^{\text{local}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>local</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}^{\text{local}}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively.
<math id="S4.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{r,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{r,g}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{r,l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{r,l}</annotation></semantics></math> are the outputs of <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{r}^{\text{global}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi><mtext>global</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{r}^{\text{global}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{r}^{\text{local}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi><mtext>local</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{r}^{\text{local}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Tags are omitted because every tensor access refers to the final result of that memory location.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The intuition of why this rewrite gives the correct result is the following:
in split-k global section, <span id="S4.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">s_sum_global</span> (which sums over <span id="S4.SS3.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sum_l</span>)
does not read from <span id="S4.SS3.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sum_l</span> too early like in rolling update.
<span id="S4.SS3.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">s_sum_global</span> executes entirely after the <span id="S4.SS3.p6.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">s_sum_local</span> loop nest.
The only correctness issue is that the values in <span id="S4.SS3.p6.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sum_l</span> are themselves wrong,
because they use incorrect row-max result <span id="S4.SS3.p6.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_l</span>.
Therefore, split-k update only needs to repair every incoming local sum <span id="S4.SS3.p6.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sum_l</span>
by tag-updating it to the correct row-max result <span id="S4.SS3.p6.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_g</span>,
which is exactly the rewrite in Eq. <a href="#S4.Ex14" title="In 4.3. Split-K Update ‣ 4. Template-Guided Optimizer ‣ Neptune: Advanced ML Operator Fusion for Locality and Parallelism on GPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Split-k update provides different tradeoffs from rolling update: split-k offers more parallelism
at the cost of a global synchronization in the middle of the program.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span><span id="S5.2" class="ltx_text">Translating from Loop-scalar IR to Tile IR</span></h2>

<figure id="S5.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
