<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the inductive hypothesis is true for <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{next}(\boldsymbol{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>next</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒋</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{next}(\boldsymbol{j})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">By induction, the theorem is true for all <math id="A4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{j}\in\mathcal{D}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒋</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{j}\in\mathcal{D}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
